 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-075: Exp4328 Either Reproduces ka59 L1 Or Records An Honest E3 Partial
 **Description:** Running Exp 4328 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_ka59` when the local ka59 simulator is absent, writes `success_e3_ka59_L1_reproduced` only when an induced-model plan is executed without trusting a divergent model and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` independently reaches at least L1 offline, or writes `complete_e3_ka59_partial_model_<acc>` when the bounded model-refinement/planning attempt does not reach the reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `offline_reproduced=true`, `reproduced_levels>=1`, `plan_executed=true`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world-model hash, plan, and reproduction result. A partial run MUST set `offline_reproduced=false`, `reproduced_levels=0`, preserve the world-model path and hash, persist the best verifier accuracy, and record the residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-076: ARC-AGI-3 E3 Executable World Model Exp4329 tr87 And ft09 Offline Attempt
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4329 as an offline, no-leaderboard E3 executable-world-model attempt over both deep-tail games `tr87` and `ft09`, checkpointing each game independently so one game cannot dominate the task window. It MUST first confirm that `environment_files/tr87/` and `environment_files/ft09/` are non-empty, that `python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py` imports, and that the task performs no TRM training and does not modify `scripts/research_conductor.py`; if both offline environments are missing it MUST write `honest_verdict="blocked_offline_env_missing_tr87_ft09"` and stop, while if only one is missing it MUST proceed with the other and record the missing game's blocked scorecard. For each available game, the workflow MUST use `results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py` as the induced model deliverable, score verifier reproduction accuracy over offline `collect_transitions(<game>)` data, print and persist per-round verifier accuracy with the game id, execute any induced-model plan only through the real offline environment, and accept a game solve only when `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` reports at least one reproduced level. If the bounded per-game budget ends without such a reproduced solve, it MUST still write an honest per-game partial with the best verifier accuracy and a residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap in `ops/verifier_gaps.md`. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4329_e3_executable_world_model_tr87_ft09.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `per_game_scorecard`, `reproduced_levels_total`, `verifier_is_oracle`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, and `reproducibility_checksum`, with `reproduced_levels_total` and `verifier_is_oracle` emitted as bare values rather than principle-wrapped dictionaries. The artifact field principles SHALL be exactly: `honest_verdict` = `Terminal-prefixed (success_e3_tr87_ft09_<n>_L1_reproduced or complete_e3_tr87_ft09_partial). Any reproduced L1 OR an honest partial per game is progress.`; `per_game_scorecard` = `Per game (tr87, ft09): offline_reproduced + reproduced_levels + best verifier_accuracy + world_model_sha256 -- breadth-of-progress, guards the one-game-dominates failure mode.`; `reproduced_levels_total` = `BARE int: total offline-reproduced levels across tr87+ft09 this task -- the +1+ incremental-progress unit.`; `verifier_is_oracle` = `BARE bool=true -- the SOLVES are execution-grounded; ARC progress, NOT a moat headline.`; `preconditions_checked` = `Records the per-game offline-env presence + harness import + TRM-stand-down; pre-empts the silent-missing-resource fabrication mode.`; `random_seed` = `Determinism precondition for the induction + planning.`; `reproducibility_checksum` = `Hash of the world models + the plans + the reproduce() results; lets a third party re-run.`
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-076: Exp4329 Checkpoints tr87 And ft09 With Reproduced L1 Or Honest Partials
+**Description:** Running Exp 4329 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_tr87_ft09` when both local simulators are absent, writes `success_e3_tr87_ft09_<n>_L1_reproduced` when one or both games independently satisfy `offline_reproduced=true` and `reproduced_levels>=1` via `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()`, or writes `complete_e3_tr87_ft09_partial` when the bounded model-refinement/planning attempts do not reach any reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `reproduced_levels_total>=1`, preserve a `per_game_scorecard` for both `tr87` and `ft09`, set `verifier_is_oracle=true`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from both world-model hashes, plans, and reproduction results. A partial run MUST set unsolved games to `offline_reproduced=false`, preserve each available game's world-model path and hash, persist the best verifier accuracy, and record each residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap. A one-missing-env run MUST still produce a scorecard row for the missing game and proceed with the present game without submitting to the leaderboard.
